  * - A press is a button going down, or a trigger rising from below
  *   kTriggerThreshold; a trigger's latch keeps the highest value it reached.
  * - The first read after the press shows it, and so does every read within
- *   kHoldNs of the press (a game that reads a pad twice in one frame sees it
- *   both times). After that it is gone.
- * - A press still held at a read is simply the pad's state: the latch drops it.
+ *   kHoldNs of that first read (a game that reads a pad several times in one
+ *   frame sees it every time). After that it is gone.
+ *   [cod3 0323] Was: within kHoldNs (4 ms) of the press itself. A press that
+ *   ended between two frames' reads was then shown to whichever read came
+ *   first, and only to it: with two readers a frame (Call of Duty 3 reads the
+ *   pad from several places in a frame, and the port's cutscene skip reads it
+ *   too), the read that builds the game's input often saw it released. At 20
+ *   fps a 20 ms tap reached the game about one time in seven (rexglue-native
+ *   thread2, the scripted pad). The window now starts at the first read that
+ *   shows it and lasts 25 ms: every read of that frame sees it (a frame's reads
+ *   come a few ms apart on the game's thread), and at 144 fps the same press
+ *   shows for 3-4 frames as one short continuous press, so a toggle still sees
+ *   one edge and nothing doubles.
+ * - A press still held at a read is simply the pad's state. [cod3 0323] That read
+ *   also starts its window: let go within it, the reads left in it still show it
+ *   (a frame's second reader); a hold longer than the window is never lengthened.
  * - Nothing is delayed: a read never shows less than the pad as it is.
  *
  * Plain values only (no SDK types), so the drivers and a unit test share it.
@@ -29,8 +42,12 @@
 
 class PressLatch {
  public:
-  // Reads closer together than this after a press all show it.
-  static constexpr uint64_t kHoldNs = 4'000'000;
+  // Reads within this of the first read that shows a press all show it ([cod3 0323] 25 ms; was 4 ms from the press).
+  static constexpr uint64_t kHoldNs = 25'000'000;
+  // [cod3 0323] A press the pad itself shows at a read: let go within this of that read, the reads left in it still
+  // show it (the frame's other readers, 0-1 ms apart in Call of Duty 3); short, so a hold is lengthened by at most
+  // this, and only a press shorter than it from the first read that saw it.
+  static constexpr uint64_t kSeenHeldNs = 8'000'000;
   // XInput's trigger threshold (rex/input/state_merge.h's kTriggerThreshold).
   static constexpr uint8_t kTriggerPressed = 30;
 
@@ -39,7 +56,7 @@
     const uint16_t down = static_cast<uint16_t>(after & ~before);
     for (int i = 0; i < 16; ++i) {
       if (down & (1u << i)) {
